{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon","id":453086,"title":"What if a group of Lesser Immortals wanted to be a full fledged Pantheon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-22T13:24:17-07:00","id":453086,"title":"What if a group of Lesser Immortals wanted to be a full fledged Pantheon?","content":"Basic idea, a group of lesser Immortals and disaffected scions have come together. They've set them selves up as a pantheon, they intend to strive<br /> against the Titans, and they've managed to gain the use of the Old Atlantean PSP as their own. (Their virtues are Conviction, Expression, Intelect, and Valor). They've shown they aren't Titan corrupted and Fate seems to say they aren't to be attacked or slain without just reason.<br /> <br /> The Pantheon has been clever and gotten a very talented author (also a lesser Imortal) to write them up as Science fiction Characters. The pantheon of an interstellar empire! They've gotten a series of really good novels written which tell the Mythology of their fictional empire. They depict a fictional religion drawn out of the best/noblest ideals of Buddhism, Chritianity, Bahai, and Daoism. They've also gotten a series of graphic novels printed and have gotten some good movies made as well. They are very real and interesting to their fanbase. And they are intending to produce more films, books, graphic novels, a TV series on basic cable, and record albums.<br /> <br /> Reactions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 03-29-2015, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T16:36:10-07:00","id":453345,"title":"","content":"This is largely a matter of context. I imagine there will be Pantheons that cry foul. Some may even try to shut the whole operation down.<br /> I'd say in the end the group would be distrusted but given due respect, gods that they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T17:46:06-07:00","id":455062,"title":"","content":"...Did you just describe Star Wars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T19:54:44-07:00","id":455270,"title":"","content":"Why do they need a writer to tell fictional stories about them? Do they sit around eating Cheetos instead of going out and doing godly stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:49:34-07:00","id":455964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=455270#post455270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do they need a writer to tell fictional stories about them? Do they sit around eating Cheetos instead of going out and doing godly stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>According the the rulebooks Gods gain something from the stories told. Besides powerfully told stories can alter the perceptions of those who hear them. Think of the impacts on society from the sttories of Twain, Dickens, Balzac, Zola, Tolstoy, and so many others. A powerfully told story and change the world. We tell myths, and the myths tell us who we are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T10:04:05-07:00","id":455978,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.... I'll change the parameters of the question, between Rumor Mill and Trendsetter and Epic Socials in general, why do they need to outsource it? If they are doing godly things and they are godly sorts, the tale-tellers will arise almost entirely independently. <br /> <br /> It's like hiring someone to make comments on your outfit when you make it completely out of the reflective material off of safety vests....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T12:21:12-07:00","id":457133,"title":"","content":"Consider how important Homer and other poets are to the reputation of the Greek Pantheon? Having fine poets praise you is important to spreading both the Deity's Legend and to spreading the ideals they stand for. Inspiring humans to embrace their values is a vital part of what the Gods seek to do. The arts are a powerful way to promote ideas and ideals. Sure, &quot;Xenna Warrior Princess&quot; was a campy TV show. But when asked by someone she'd rescued, after he'd tried to kill her, &quot;What do you expect of me?&quot; Tell me her answer &quot;Of you, nothing, of me, nothing less.&quot; didn't powerfully pomote the ideals of the Greek pantheon?<br /> <br /> Putting your message out there in a way that it reaches impressionable minds and shapes them is profoundly powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T18:22:45-07:00","id":457547,"title":"","content":"Seems like a God with Epic Charisma 9 and a softly spoken word during a TV interview wouldn't ever need a Homer. People will tell stories about gods doing godly things. We're tale-telling critters. Look at the things we care about so much right now without gods: the Kardashians, what we just ate, sports, movies, RPGs... What would people be talking about if actual GODS were striding around doing godly things. What the gods DID. Not what some dude wrote about them in a comic book. <br /> <br /> The Greek Gods didn't need Homer. In fact, if anything, Homer and Snurri and their lot really cramped the gods' style. Homer wasn't an embedded reporter during the Trojan War, nor was he a crewman of Odysseus's (luckily for him). He sang about things AFTER they were long over. Based on the tales passed down from the long ago. When the gods weren't out being super impressive anymore and were cooling their heels back on Olympus avoiding any more Fatebinding. <br /> <br /> If the group is out and about doing godly things, people will probably be reporting it, showing it on TV, talking about it on Twitter and Facebook, Instagraming away, writing fan fic, etc. etc. but that will all pale before the deeds proper. Gods don't need press agents all that much. What image massaging they might want can be accomplished effortlessly with Epic Socials and/or a few relevant Knacks. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T19:26:24-07:00","id":457593,"title":"","content":"I'm more confused about how and why they've &quot;gained the use of&quot; the <i>Atlantean</i> PSP? Why? Out of character shortcut to avoid writing a new PSP? Or are they supposed to somehow be connected to that craziness of the Atlantean Pantheon?<br /> <br /> How is their &quot;religion&quot; going to work when it's demonstrably false? There are no space ships. No aliens. They're <i>not</i> doing these things. Why not tell stories about what they're <i>actually</i> doing? <br /> <br /> I just don't really understand what the goal is here. A low-level Pantheon is really... just more of a club. Which is cool, there can totally be a club of supernatural creatures and Scions united by their love of science fiction, striving to develop new technology and propel Humanity to the Stars! That's great. I love that. But why are they trying to create a fictional religion instead of starting a <i>real</i> one, based on their <i>real</i> Legendary Deeds and Miraculous Accomplishments? How come they're stealing the PSP of some ancient, corrupted, fictional Gods instead of forging their own, Boon by Boon? If they want to be a Pantheon, they're going to need to drive their Legend up, assure their parents/patrons that they're <i>no threat</i> (they're a threat) and that their new Pantheon won't cost their forebears power (it totally will) and that Fate supports them (it might). <br /> <br /> So I can see this being something cool... just not as you've presented it so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T22:00:13-07:00","id":460684,"title":"","content":"I've been told both the Overworld and the Underworld are infinite, so there is plenty of room to carve out new Pantheon territories. Except I've also been told most of the pantheons don't like each other very much, so you'd have that to worry about in addition to the Titans.<br /> <br /> <br /> On another note, I quite like the mental image of a bunch of gods sitting around playing games and eating chips all day while hiring people to write their legends for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-29-2015, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T00:02:36-07:00","id":460782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=460684#post460684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, I quite like the mental image of a bunch of gods sitting around playing games and eating chips all day while hiring people to write their legends for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... honestly cannot think of a less appealing group of deities. Maybe as some kind of comedic take on the uselessness of Gods? Or a commentary on decadence following success? Like, they USED to be awesome and now they're just sitting on their butts, eating chips, being losers while someone else makes up stories about them? But... a group that never <i>did</i> anything and just spins stories about deeds they've never done? No.. I can't see wanting to play them, play their followers, or be involved in a story about them except as objects of contempt and derision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T05:57:02-07:00","id":460961,"title":"","content":"Well obviously they aren't going to become gods in the first place if they just sit around. But the idea could hold some degree of merit. Especially since this pantheon is <i>new</i> and inexperienced.<br /> <br /> I could see them being portrayed as having the mindset of most mortals who aspire to godhood. They think once they've joined the powers that be, they're above reproach or questioning, so there's no longer a reason to work for their accomplishments which they believe they are entitled to by right. It isn't until after they become gods and encounter the true bulk of the Titan forces that they realize being a god has a lot more responsibilities than kicking back and ruling the universe all day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T09:10:32-07:00","id":461087,"title":"","content":"Are these guys Gods yet? As in Legend 12 types? If not, how are they a pantheon? Can you be a pantheon if any Scions you sire belong to their grandparents? Are they as much a pretend pantheon as they are pretend heroes?<br /> <br /> This sounds like a band of Scions that forfeited doing anything mythical to become slackers and have some dupe foist off lies about them on a public used to tall tales and special effects movies. In which case, there should be much in the way of parental thrashings and some ominous grumblings from thwarted Fate. Why would Fate be okay with this bunch? The don't DO anything. Unless their Fate is to do nothing of any important but hang out. Maybe they are a decoy for some band of Scions that actually do shit?<br /> <br /> And I'm still not seeing where Scire comes into it. Did they just happen to find scrolls about it or something? Presumably self-translating or perhaps able to download themselves into a teaching tool that masquerades as a computer game? (You just leveled up! Congrats, you now have Scire 3!) Otherwise, I can't see them bothering to translate something that would be difficult. (Plus all the grease stains from the potato chops, rings from set down energy drinks, etc on the ancient sacred scrolls.) These guys don't seem like the types to do something as difficult as find a dead Under or Overworld, pass all the tests, face all the challenges and seize the secrets of a dead, lost pantheon from the horrors of what the remnants have become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T13:17:25-07:00","id":461382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=460782#post460782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... honestly cannot think of a less appealing group of deities. Maybe as some kind of comedic take on the uselessness of Gods? Or a commentary on decadence following success? Like, they USED to be awesome and now they're just sitting on their butts, eating chips, being losers while someone else makes up stories about them? But... a group that never <i>did</i> anything and just spins stories about deeds they've never done? No.. I can't see wanting to play them, play their followers, or be involved in a story about them except as objects of contempt and derision.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they don't just sit around and play games. They are active in the world. They have the stories to enhance and generate Legend and promote the virtues (Conviction, Expression, Intelect, Valor) they champion. The art works and stories are a tool to reshape society to make it more resistant to the Titans and their warped ideals. They do alot besides hire actors to play them and spin stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T13:25:49-07:00","id":461387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=461087#post461087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are these guys Gods yet? As in Legend 12 types? If not, how are they a pantheon? Can you be a pantheon if any Scions you sire belong to their grandparents? Are they as much a pretend pantheon as they are pretend heroes?<br /> This sounds like a band of Scions that forfeited doing anything mythical to become slackers and have some dupe foist off lies about them on a public used to tall tales and special effects movies. In which case, there should be much in the way of parental thrashings and some ominous grumblings from thwarted Fate. Why would Fate be okay with this bunch? The don't DO anything. Unless their Fate is to do nothing of any important but hang out. Maybe they are a decoy for some band of Scions that actually do shit?<br /> And I'm still not seeing where Scire comes into it. Did they just happen to find scrolls about it or something? Presumably self-translating or perhaps able to download themselves into a teaching tool that masquerades as a computer game? (You just leveled up! Congrats, you now have Scire 3!) Otherwise, I can't see them bothering to translate something that would be difficult. (Plus all the grease stains from the potato chops, rings from set down energy drinks, etc on the ancient sacred scrolls.) These guys don't seem like the types to do something as difficult as find a dead Under or Overworld, pass all the tests, face all the challenges and seize the secrets of a dead, lost pantheon from the horrors of what the remnants have become.</div> </div> </div> </div>The stories are vectors to promote values and ideals. Concider the Myths and tales used by the older Gods to promote their ideals and visions. Educating the masses in order to change society to make it more just, fairer, freer, more equiable, is an important task. Reread the describtions of the Pantheons in the Scion: Hero book. The Loa work to create harmonious homes, the Aseir work to balance individual and society, can't you see how the stories told to people, and the values expressed in those stories promote social values? This pantheon is acting to fight off the Titans. And like all the other pantheons, they use the Arts as a tool in that fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T14:16:10-07:00","id":461437,"title":"","content":"Are you alleging that the Aesir just had Snorri on retainer? Same with the Celestial Bureaucracy and Cheng'en? The Dodekatheon and Homer? <br /> <br /> But all those guys (plus several more) all were harkening back to &quot;days of yore&quot;, retelling stories of gods that did things when gods were out doing things. Which was before their time. And probably are something that make the gods in questions rub their temples and sigh a lot, since, not matter what REALLY happened, those stories are weighing them down with Fatebinding, which is pretty much solely a negative thing. <br /> <br /> Again, are your guys Legend 12? Or at least Legend 9? If not, how is this not a &quot;band with a 'tude&quot; instead of a Pantheon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T20:52:30-07:00","id":461836,"title":"","content":"I guess I just don't see why they're writing about <i>fiction</i> when they could be writing about <i>real</i> legendary deeds and <i>real</i> miracles? Now, I could totally see a Scion author that writes the most amazing fiction ever, and uses that as <i>one of their real deeds</i> to inspire... but the idea of a whole &quot;Pantheon&quot; based on fiction just seems.. weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T12:37:42-07:00","id":462609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=461836#post461836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I just don't see why they're writing about <i>fiction</i> when they could be writing about <i>real</i> legendary deeds and <i>real</i> miracles? Now, I could totally see a Scion author that writes the most amazing fiction ever, and uses that as <i>one of their real deeds</i> to inspire... but the idea of a whole &quot;Pantheon&quot; based on fiction just seems.. weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't based on Fiction, they are useing fiction to spread their ideals. Older Pantheons could simply inspire and take their time, these guys need to move fast. They are acting physically against the manifestations of the Titans, but they also use the arts to spread ideas that make society more resistant to the Titans. Modern times, modern methods, same goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 03-31-2015, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T14:49:28-07:00","id":462692,"title":"","content":"Kinda like using comic books to promote certain ideals that represent virtues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T20:58:21-07:00","id":463066,"title":"","content":"I'm still just stumped as to why they're writing about <i>fictional things</i> when they could be inspiring people with their <i>actual</i> legends. Reading about the guy who <i>actually</i> defeated an army of zombies is way cooler than reading one about some made up dude who defeated space aliens. That's why people love the idea of &quot;based on a true story&quot; narratives. And in this case, there is <i>actual legendary stuff</i> happening. Giants, monsters, zombies, gods, centaurs! I just really can't wrap my head around why they'd choose to promote their ideals and virtues using fiction instead of reality, when reality is way cooler anyway. It isn't like fiction offers something that they can't just go <i>do</i>. They're demigods. They can be way cooler than Superman or Green Lantern or Star Wars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T05:56:47-07:00","id":463375,"title":"","content":"Legends take dilution and forming them differently to take in. Or to put it another way; A lot more people knew about Thor and what he represented than this Percy Jackson fellow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T13:35:50-07:00","id":463834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=463066#post463066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still just stumped as to why they're writing about <i>fictional things</i> when they could be inspiring people with their <i>actual</i> legends. Reading about the guy who <i>actually</i> defeated an army of zombies is way cooler than reading one about some made up dude who defeated space aliens. That's why people love the idea of &quot;based on a true story&quot; narratives. And in this case, there is <i>actual legendary stuff</i> happening. Giants, monsters, zombies, gods, centaurs! I just really can't wrap my head around why they'd choose to promote their ideals and virtues using fiction instead of reality, when reality is way cooler anyway. It isn't like fiction offers something that they can't just go <i>do</i>. They're demigods. They can be way cooler than Superman or Green Lantern or Star Wars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting the message out is important. Positive images of the future that motivate people to act on their values because they can image a reason to have hope is important. These folks Embrace Conviction, Expression, Intelect, and Valor, as their pantheon virtues. Valor is about standing up for that which is right and just in an honnorable way. How many modern day phillosophy professors believe in honor, or that standing up for that which is right is worthwhile? Culture pessimism is the crushing bane of our age and a bane that destroys the ideal of Valor. Similarly, Intelect and Expression, without ideals to support them become hollow and false. Convictions ripped to pieces by sneering nihilists fall into dust. Stories reach into other parts of the mind and soul and fight these forces.<br /> <br /> This pantheon embraces storytelling as a weapon against the Titans. And a potent one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:35:16-07:00","id":463887,"title":"","content":"That.. does not at all address the issue of why are they telling <i>fictional</i> stories that are <i>demonstrably false</i> instead of telling their <i>actual Legends</i>?<br /> <br /> They are out there punching Giants and saving the World from zombie hordes, right? I have no problem with their approach to inspiration. That makes sense. Movies, TV shows, comics, etc. But why are they telling SciFi stories about a fictional empire when they could be <i>founding their own empire and building space ships with their god-powers? </i>They could be selling comics about <i>that</i> stuff. The <i>real</i> stuff they're actually out there <i>doing</i>. <br /> <br /> Why not have their Relics take the form of Ra-powered <i>sekhem</i> lasers and Thor-2 style viking longships that fly around on ion engines? They can inspire hope, inspire cultural change, inspire <i>anything</i> with their own powers, their own deeds, their own drive and abilities. If they want a galactic federation, <i>they can totally do that</i>. Grab some Epic Intelligence and design environmental support equipment that can sustain a colony on Mars. Or use Rainbow Bridge and some Fertility powers to <i>grow a garden on the Red Planet and move people there!</i> There are literally <i>no limits</i> in Scion.<br /> <br /> I just don't understand why this Pantheon-Band is all about telling <i>fictional</i> stories instead of just going out and <i>doin</i> things which they can then tell stories about. It confuses me. Basically I see this as Superman spending his time telling stories about Mr. AmazingMan!!... who is a character that Superman himself invented and does not actually exist. Superman could inspire a lot more people by, say, being Superman at least some of the time and then having a really savvy marketing team sell <i>his</i> story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:55:41-07:00","id":463907,"title":"","content":"All that. Yes. Well put.<br /> <br /> Also, our fiction and media are replete with characters who demonstrate Valor. Maybe a bit of a tip towards Vengeance (thanks Liam Neeson's recent oeuvre), but a LOT of good guy noble heroes out there. In comics. In movies. In comic book movies. In fiction. On TV. So, if we get our Virtues from what this pantheon is pedaling they might actually get lost in the noise of similar messages from mundane sources. (You could always use some Social Knacks to make sure your stand out I guess...) <br /> <br /> We're probably the most Expression enabled group of human in forever. Whole industries based on it. Scads of people involved in it. Look at where we're talking about all this? One small part of one small sub-industry in a society that's addicted to having all the Expression you could ever want and then some. And there's so much, you even are pretty much obligated to pick some things to like and some not or else drown in the flow! <br /> <br /> We're also surrounded by cool Intellect stuff. It's definitely there if you want it. (Vide RPGs for the most part). It may not be as ultra-cool as it was in, say, the 1960's. But then again, there is an exaltation of &quot;nerd culture&quot; that definitely has a pro-Intellect stance. Plus the biggest &quot;rags (meaning kinda nice clothes that are slightly better than most people have) to riches&quot; stories are tech billionaires. That's pro-Intellect. <br /> <br /> Conviction the Scion Virtue (not conviction the real-world virtue) is really scarey. Not sure it's something you want to encourage widely if you aren't totally 100% on board with the mission statement. Forcing people to read their comics. Burning all the other comics. Burning alive the people who read other comics. Conviction is what gets Aztecs past the squick factor of carving out people's hearts. They HAVE to. It's necessary. Their faith is RIGHT and what must be done in its name MUST BE DONE. No matter the cost. <br /> <br /> So, three of four we kinda already got and the fourth.... well, I hope their Conviction is about playing video-games, eating Cheetos and reading comics and, even then, Conviction about those things has a high potential to end... badly (for the non-gamers, haters of Cheetos and those who spurn comics).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T11:43:12-07:00","id":478151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=463907#post463907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conviction the Scion Virtue (not conviction the real-world virtue) is really scarey. Not sure it's something you want to encourage widely if you aren't totally 100% on board with the mission statement. Forcing people to read their comics. Burning all the other comics. Burning alive the people who read other comics. Conviction is what gets Aztecs past the squick factor of carving out people's hearts. They HAVE to. It's necessary. Their faith is RIGHT and what must be done in its name MUST BE DONE. No matter the cost.<br /> So, three of four we kinda already got and the fourth.... well, I hope their Conviction is about playing video-games, eating Cheetos and reading comics and, even then, Conviction about those things has a high potential to end... badly (for the non-gamers, haters of Cheetos and those who spurn comics).</div> </div> </div> </div>Suppose their convictions were about Freedom, Liberty, Justice, Fairness, Democracy, Equality, and Social Justice. They want a better world and understand that people need to restate the terms of what a better world is on a fairly regular basis. Would the other pantheons attack, support, or ignore?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T14:26:43-07:00","id":478304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=478151#post478151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Suppose their convictions were about Freedom, Liberty, Justice, Fairness, Democracy, Equality, and Social Justice. They want a better world and understand that people need to restate the terms of what a better world is on a fairly regular basis. Would the other pantheons attack, support, or ignore?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't believe in those things in EXACTLY the way they do? You have different definition? Convert or die. You have to want THEIR better world, <br /> <br /> Again, are any of these guys actually Gods? Are they just low Legend people calling themselves a pantheon? Do they have the chops to stand up to the machinations of Loki or Tezcatlipoca? If Thor gets pissed off, are they a red smear on Mjolnir or a severed head on Ares's pilum? <br /> <br /> Ignored if it's beneath the gods' threshold of annoyance. <br /> Destroyed if they gods get annoyed.<br /> Used (not supported) if there is anything worth doing that they might be able to do<br /> Played with if they look any fun. (Usually followed by &quot;Destroyed&quot; when they aren't anymore.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T16:44:08-07:00","id":478424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=478151#post478151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppose their convictions were about Freedom, Liberty, Justice, Fairness, Democracy, Equality, and Social Justice. They want a better world and understand that people need to restate the terms of what a better world is on a fairly regular basis. Would the other pantheons attack, support, or ignore?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm..the likes of Superman and Captain America have ever demonstrated such virtues time and time again. Their actions define them. If other pantheons went on attack mode, much of humanity would possibly rally behind such heroes. If the gods take issue with humanity's defensive response, then their actions may define them as villains. And I believe that humanity could and should be a wild card that could affect the gods. It most certainly wouldn't do if major governments believed that death would be a better option than tyranny under a pantheon)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T21:15:26-07:00","id":478747,"title":"","content":"And yet, the Gods can re-write human opinions, easily. An Epic Social here, an Epic Social there, and now hundreds of millions of humans no longer think the Gods are tyrants at all. Scion is not a game where humans matter in the grand scheme of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T06:27:45-07:00","id":478995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=478747#post478747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scion is not a game where humans matter in the grand scheme of things.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Only in your game.</b><br /> To me, if humans don't matter, then having a human/god hybrid doesn't matter either.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T08:44:50-07:00","id":479084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=478995#post478995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Only in your game.</b><br /> To me, if humans don't matter, then having a human/god hybrid doesn't matter either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. You can sway things however you want in your game, but the rules of Scion doesn't really support what you're saying. When you start playing or running Scion you begin to realize that humans are pretty much playthings almost right from the get-go. They can't hurt you, imprison you or negatively affect you very much at all. You can pretty much kill them, coerce them (and make them adore you for it), etc at will. As ST, if your plot depends on the Scions being challenged by humans in any way, you better have it planned out for them to automatically succeed. There are obvious exceptions, like surviving a drone strike at low Legend. But it doesn't even take Demigod level socials to walk right into the White House and make the President your lackey using Epic Socials and few common Knacks.<br /> <br /> So, out of the box/RAW, humans don't matter much.<br /> <br /> If you want them to matter, you need to do a lot of work. Figure out a way for people with non-Epics to have a chance against beings with Epic stats, Knacks and Boons. Make Fatebinding really binding. Some stuff like that. But it's a more than couple of house rules, it's a major reconstruction of the rules of the game inside and out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 04-13-2015, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T11:30:23-07:00","id":479308,"title":"","content":"The idea that humans don't matter falls apart when viewing the Aztecs (and other pantheons that demand human sacrifice). If humans don't matter there has been a lot of unnecessary murders. All for nothing unless the gods view that sort of thing as entertainment. And who goes by RAW? At demigod that again falls apart. Of course if one goes by the idea that the gods have progressed beyond ritual murder, that's an idea I like. Furthermore, if humans don't matter, then the gods shouldn't care one way or another if humans pay a little more attention to stories of other gods... <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppose their convictions were about Freedom, Liberty, Justice, Fairness, Democracy, Equality, and Social Justice. They want a better world and understand that people need to restate the terms of what a better world is on a fairly regular basis. Would the other pantheons attack, support, or ignore?</div> </div> </div> </div> To run with the idea that humans don't matter...*sigh* There could be thousands of deities that pre-date the current favorites. Such &quot;scions&quot; could be in the form of my examples of &quot;Superman&quot; and Captain America.&quot; Unknown deities could be all the support that they need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T14:52:04-07:00","id":479517,"title":"","content":"No it doesn't. Not at all. Iztli means the sacrifices are a source of Legend, but not one the Aztec gods need in a mechanical sense. Otherwise the other pantheons, in a mechanical sense, would be screwed. And they're not. So the PSP of the Aztecs gives easier access to Legend at the price of a few followers. That actually diminishes the value of human life in a particular sense. The herd is large and it would take a whole lot of killing to exhaust it. If you thinks cows really really matter to human civilization, I guess I can see your point as being internally valid, but I don't think most people see cattle or other animals we kill and eat as being vitally important and mattering in a fundamental sense.<br /> <br /> The other thing killing people does for the Aztec gods in Scion is allow them to exercise their Conviction. That's important too. Otherwise they would be getting a little tetchy. So mass human sacrifice is kinda like squeezing a stress ball for them. Once again, not really something that makes human &quot;important&quot; for most values of the word. <br /> <br /> Other than killing people as the &quot;cosmic grease&quot; to keep the universe going, people, particularly in a humanist sense, don't matter to the Aztec gods. They really aren't a good set of candidates for gods who give a crap about people. They are pretty much the poster children for the opposite in many of the fundamental ways in which the term &quot;people matter&quot; applies in Western culture. <br /> <br /> If you want humans to matter in your Scion game as a ST, you can state that to your players. If you want to play in a Scion game and you want humans to matter, you can have your character act that way. I certainly have and it was a significant point of conflict with another player whose character thought that murder-suicide Fight Club cults were the go to way to &quot;harvest&quot; more einherjar for Valhalla and make his dad proud. The problem you are going to face as a ST is that is almost every way, humans DON'T matter a fig in the context of the rules. So, at best, they are &quot;pets&quot; for the more humanist godlings. There is no mechanism in the game to punish gods for being 'inhumane&quot; in any holistic sense. The closest you can get is Virtues and each and every one of them, including the &quot;good&quot; ones has a very very dark side to it. There are little to no places in the game for humans to be of any real assistance or to provide anything resembling a threat. <br /> <br /> Remember, aside from a few off hand and as out of place as Hardness comments, Scion doesn't connect human worship up with empowering gods. (YAY!) In fact, at best, mortals make gods &quot;itchy&quot; when they start affecting them through individual and mass Fatebindings.<br /> <br /> Can you find any solid evidence in the rules to back up your contentions that in the game as written, not your personal take on it, gods are supposed to value humans in some fundamental way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T15:08:06-07:00","id":479526,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that Scion isn't something that most play by the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T11:10:46-07:00","id":481414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=479517#post479517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No it doesn't. Not at all. Iztli means the sacrifices are a source of Legend, but not one the Aztec gods need in a mechanical sense. Otherwise the other pantheons, in a mechanical sense, would be screwed. And they're not. So the PSP of the Aztecs gives easier access to Legend at the price of a few followers. That actually diminishes the value of human life in a particular sense. The herd is large and it would take a whole lot of killing to exhaust it. If you thinks cows really really matter to human civilization, I guess I can see your point as being internally valid, but I don't think most people see cattle or other animals we kill and eat as being vitally important and mattering in a fundamental sense.<br /> The other thing killing people does for the Aztec gods in Scion is allow them to exercise their Conviction. That's important too. Otherwise they would be getting a little tetchy. So mass human sacrifice is kinda like squeezing a stress ball for them. Once again, not really something that makes human &quot;important&quot; for most values of the word.<br /> Other than killing people as the &quot;cosmic grease&quot; to keep the universe going, people, particularly in a humanist sense, don't matter to the Aztec gods. They really aren't a good set of candidates for gods who give a crap about people. They are pretty much the poster children for the opposite in many of the fundamental ways in which the term &quot;people matter&quot; applies in Western culture.<br /> If you want humans to matter in your Scion game as a ST, you can state that to your players. If you want to play in a Scion game and you want humans to matter, you can have your character act that way. I certainly have and it was a significant point of conflict with another player whose character thought that murder-suicide Fight Club cults were the go to way to &quot;harvest&quot; more einherjar for Valhalla and make his dad proud. The problem you are going to face as a ST is that is almost every way, humans DON'T matter a fig in the context of the rules. So, at best, they are &quot;pets&quot; for the more humanist godlings. There is no mechanism in the game to punish gods for being 'inhumane&quot; in any holistic sense. The closest you can get is Virtues and each and every one of them, including the &quot;good&quot; ones has a very very dark side to it. There are little to no places in the game for humans to be of any real assistance or to provide anything resembling a threat.<br /> Remember, aside from a few off hand and as out of place as Hardness comments, Scion doesn't connect human worship up with empowering gods. (YAY!) In fact, at best, mortals make gods &quot;itchy&quot; when they start affecting them through individual and mass Fatebindings.<br /> Can you find any solid evidence in the rules to back up your contentions that in the game as written, not your personal take on it, gods are supposed to value humans in some fundamental way?</div> </div> </div> </div>I take it that you give Stalin, Robesperie, and Hitler, more credit for Conviction than you would for FDR and his Eleanore, Lincoln, Jurez, Mother Jones, Mandella, or Dr. King?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T10:34:28-07:00","id":482515,"title":"","content":"Absolutely. <br /> <br /> The later list of &quot;good guys&quot; may have had &quot;the courage of their convictions&quot; but they had neither Courage nor Conviction the Scion Virtues as described in RAW. The first three have something more like Scion Conviction. Look at the description - &quot;take any measures necessary to further her cause or take action to further her beliefs&quot;, you get dice adds &quot;to commit heinous acts in support of their belief&quot;, you have to fail a Virtue roll or spend a Willpower &quot;refuse to perform an action that will benefit their cause (even if it results in the suffering of others)&quot;. Note &quot;any measure necessary&quot;, &quot;heinous acts&quot;, &quot;result in suffering&quot;. <br /> <br /> Like almost all the other Virtues, it may share a name with something identified as &quot;virtuous&quot;, but they are NOT the same thing. What is normally thought of as the virtuous behavior associated with that word is usually a part of the behaviors that characterize the Scion Virtue, that it encourages or that it discourages, but there are always, other, darker parts of them.<br /> <br /> Conviction, as a case in point, definitely dances with the dark side quite openly. It's there on the face of it. (Not like Courage, which sounds good on paper, but really encompasses not only bravery, but bravado, foolhardiness, being a braggart, having a very thin skin where certain insults are concerned.)<br /> <br /> So, if you want Conviction, Courage, etc. to mean what they normally mean when used, you need to, once again, <i>change the rules</i>. You need to edit those lists and change some of the fundamental assumptions of the game, which starts from the fact that the orginal meaning of the word &quot;hero&quot; in Greek doesn't have very much to do with being a &quot;good guy&quot; at all. Heroes can be right bastards, they just have to be greater than human. And thereby take out some gods or pantheons as playable options, because much of mythology is NOT about the good guys beating the bad guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T11:29:53-07:00","id":482602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=479517#post479517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, aside from a few off hand and as out of place as Hardness comments, Scion doesn't connect human worship up with empowering gods. (YAY!) In fact, at best, mortals make gods &quot;itchy&quot; when they start affecting them through individual and mass Fatebindings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in 1e, and not in the base setting of 2e, no.<br /> <br /> Although it's worth noting that Fatebindings and perception <i>can </i>slightly alter a god's characteristics or inadvertently lock them into a mode of behavior, which is a reason the gods shy away from interacting with mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T12:59:48-07:00","id":482656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=482602#post482602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not in 1e, and not in the base setting of 2e, no.<br /> <br /> Although it's worth noting that Fatebindings and perception <i>can </i>slightly alter a god's characteristics or inadvertently lock them into a mode of behavior, which is a reason the gods shy away from interacting with mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are those &quot;no's&quot; disagreements with the points I was making or agreeing with them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T18:22:52-07:00","id":483008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=482656#post482656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are those &quot;no's&quot; disagreements with the points I was making or agreeing with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreeing with you, though clarifying a point - Fatebinding in the setting makes the gods a little more than <i>itchy</i>, it binds their behavior to a degree where they find it unreasonable to function. I mean, clearly the mechanics don't back up the setting elements, but if we start in on that point we'll be here all day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T07:18:30-07:00","id":483522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=482515#post482515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely.<br /> <br /> The later list of &quot;good guys&quot; may have had &quot;the courage of their convictions&quot; but they had neither Courage nor Conviction the Scion Virtues as described in RAW. The first three have something more like Scion Conviction. Look at the description - &quot;take any measures necessary to further her cause or take action to further her beliefs&quot;, you get dice adds &quot;to commit heinous acts in support of their belief&quot;, you have to fail a Virtue roll or spend a Willpower &quot;refuse to perform an action that will benefit their cause (even if it results in the suffering of others)&quot;. Note &quot;any measure necessary&quot;, &quot;heinous acts&quot;, &quot;result in suffering&quot;.<br /> <br /> Like almost all the other Virtues, it may share a name with something identified as &quot;virtuous&quot;, but they are NOT the same thing. What is normally thought of as the virtuous behavior associated with that word is usually a part of the behaviors that characterize the Scion Virtue, that it encourages or that it discourages, but there are always, other, darker parts of them.<br /> <br /> Conviction, as a case in point, definitely dances with the dark side quite openly. It's there on the face of it. (Not like Courage, which sounds good on paper, but really encompasses not only bravery, but bravado, foolhardiness, being a braggart, having a very thin skin where certain insults are concerned.)<br /> <br /> So, if you want Conviction, Courage, etc. to mean what they normally mean when used, you need to, once again, <i>change the rules</i>. You need to edit those lists and change some of the fundamental assumptions of the game, which starts from the fact that the orginal meaning of the word &quot;hero&quot; in Greek doesn't have very much to do with being a &quot;good guy&quot; at all. Heroes can be right bastards, they just have to be greater than human. And thereby take out some gods or pantheons as playable options, because much of mythology is NOT about the good guys beating the bad guys.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its worth noting (and is hopefully explained in 2E as you would be surprised a the amount of people who think otherwise) that many of the pantheon virtues are not just extreme behaviors of divinity and legend, but are actual Virtues as seen by different cultures and religions. Your description of Courage is right on the nose for the Norse conception of the Virtue of Courage, but is seen by most people today as somewhere between psychotic and arrogant due to the different moral codes inherent in Christianity. Courage is not connected with &quot;Morals&quot; as we would today understand them, its technically possible for a Pedophile to engage in and even be a paragon of &quot;Courage&quot; The Virtue. Martial correctness in a moral manner is mostly covered by the Greek Virtue of Valor.<br /> <br /> In lots of cultures, heinous acts committed due to Duties, Loyalties or Convictions were considered to be honorable and venerable, even if the actual action would not normally have been. While I guess you can do anything you want at your own table, expecting mythological Gods and Heroes to conform to our present cultural values and morals is not going to work out too well. Sometimes people come off as Evil when they were considered to be paragons of proper behavior in their society, sometimes people thought to be funny or harmless were considered deeply disturbing or even criminal in their own society, and sometimes Deities are just represented to be Bad dudes because the concept that a Divinity should be forthright and moral is an entirely alien concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T08:17:27-07:00","id":483541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=483522#post483522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its worth noting (and is hopefully explained in 2E as you would be surprised a the amount of people who think otherwise) that many of the pantheon virtues are not just extreme behaviors of divinity and legend, but are actual Virtues as seen by different cultures and religions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back when civilizations were still in their various beginning stages...yes, I agree.<br /> I look back to when I was a child and see all the mistakes I made. I learned from them and eventually did mature and grow. (and discovered so many new ways to make mistakes..dammit)<br /> But I should hope that civilizations and their respective pantheons can do the same. (Of course, that's probably not relevant to the game..*sigh*) Times change...and keeping things as they were thousands of years ago...if not longer, just doesn't make sense to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T09:12:45-07:00","id":483600,"title":"","content":"That is emphatically another example of the same bias, based on a false equivalency. Cultures are not humans who age through various stages of moral development (in fact, much of what humans consider to be moral or ethical at any point in their lives is completely culture bound. We definitely do things in modern American culture that are absolutely abhorent to other current cultures, even those we would consider to be &quot;on the same wavelength&quot; and would be equally heretical/disgusting/naive/laughable to previous cultures. Modern America is not the perfected end result of some moral evolution of humanity. First, that's not how evolution works at all. It has nothing to do with it. Nothing is more evolved than anything else. All things are equally evolved as they are all the end result of the same process applied across the board. Some traits, some cultures, some ideas might be more adaptive in the current situation, but, when the situation changes, the selective pressures change and what was adaptive yesterday might get you dead today. In fact, as far as most professional academics today are concerned, there are piles and piles and piles of evidence that indicate that modern Western culture is, in fact, malapative in the extreme on several fronts. We aren't just &quot;not better&quot; than previous cultures, we may be worse off. Actually we ARE worse off in terms of things like free-time to resource acquisition and many other fronts. (For an example, think about dishwashers. They consume more time and resources by far than just washing your dishes by hand. Think about it. For virtually all commercially available dishwashers, you have to handwash the dishes ANYWAY, then put them in the machine, run the machine with all those associated additional costs, then, most likely hand dry most if not all of them ANYWAY, then put them away.... You haven't saved anything. You have wasted a lot of time and effort and the only real difference is that, for a little while, your dishes are warm....)<br /> <br /> The question in terms of the context of Scion is whether the pantheons of ancient cultures are going to change over time. There is some evidence either way, but the balance of the evidence in RAW is that the pantheons are going to remain static representations of some view of their source culture. The Virtues, Fatebinding, etc. all tie directly into that. Where change could have been manifested, e.g. in places such as some gradual shift of the attitudes in the gods over time, like, say, the Greek portrayals of the Dodekatheon vs. the Roman portrayals of the same, that idea was never addressed. And though negative evidence isn't as dispostive as positive evidence, it is still evidence. [Caveat: I do know that things are/might be changing in Scion 2.0, but for those of us out here in the wilderness hearing only the whispers of the songs being sung at the designers' campfires, RAW and discussions of House Rules are all we've got to work with until we get something playable.] It's definitely a viewpoint that has some solid backing on both the practical and most esoteric sides of academics investigations into the same issues. Pantheons and religions are the place where the most fervent viewpoints on cultural values are steadfastly held to. They are the core of cultural identity. As the founder of sociology (and arguably, one of the founders of anthropology as well) Emile Durkheim said, religion is the mirror where a culture goes to look at it's perfected self (both paraphrased and translated from French). <br /> <br /> If you, in your game, want the pantheons to adhere to Western cultural norms, kudos. Go for it. I admit that, even after decades of training in cultural relativism and past cultures, when I really think about Aztec, Greek &amp; Roman, Norse, etc. varieties of human sacrifice, it seems pretty horrible to me. Particularly the accompanying cannibalism among the Aztecs (and the sheer, almost industrialized SCALE, of their sacrifices). Also, the institutionalized incest among Egyptian royalty. (But neither is worse in any way than the blood-drinking in Vampire, overall.) For me, having those be totally acceptable things to your character's parents is part of what Scion is about; the struggle between generations. (Also backed up in the books by having the LAST generational conflict flare back up.). But that doesn't have to be the way you do it in your own game. If you are playing in someone else's game and they are hewing close to the rules, you need to be upfront about it, because there definitely will be the kinds of problems that tear bands apart and turn them into arch-nemeses who will do anything to destroy their former comrade(s) and all their works. (And how appropriately mythic is that? A whole ton of a lot...)<br /> <br /> And, once again, if you are going to RUN a Scion game, you are going to need to put this into your House Rules and be pretty explicit about it, as it is a change in direction from the base game. Someone who just reads RAW might or might not clue in otherwise and you might have some very disappointed players. I've already identified some of the areas you are going to have to change to make your personalized version of Scion based on how you perceive the core conflicts of the game - change the Virtues to the point of eliminating them, reconfigure Fatebinding so the gods don't end up being forced to be the kind of jerks you want them to have &quot;evolved&quot; away from, etc. You might even want to institute some kind of Humanity stat so you can punish backsliders or those who choose the older and darker ways. I dunno what else might work, but it might be deserving of a thread of it's own, separate from the issues of this one. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T11:17:57-07:00","id":483756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=483541#post483541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back when civilizations were still in their various beginning stages...yes, I agree.<br /> I look back to when I was a child and see all the mistakes I made. I learned from them and eventually did mature and grow. (and discovered so many new ways to make mistakes..dammit)<br /> But I should hope that civilizations and their respective pantheons can do the same. (Of course, that's probably not relevant to the game..*sigh*) Times change...and keeping things as they were thousands of years ago...if not longer, just doesn't make sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't Spend a whole lot of time on it as Ajax covered it nicely, but you should understand that what your saying is extremely offensive and flat ignorant. Current Western values are largely a complex interwoven pattern of Ancient Semitic morality and Greco-Roman social thinking bound into a coherent form by Christianity. This was historically impressed on much of the world through warfare, oppression and other unsavory tactics to either kill outright, or force underground, Indigenous modes of thought and beliefs. No, Your cultural beliefs and morality is not the pinnacle of thought and its certainly not the only viable way. Stating that every other religious or cultural value is either Primitive or childlike is not only absurd, but ethnocentric and offensive to anyone who happens to not be a Western European Christian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T11:46:24-07:00","id":483783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I won't Spend a whole lot of time on it as Ajax covered it nicely, but you should understand that what your saying is extremely offensive and flat ignorant.</div> </div> </div> </div> In what way? (Walls of text tend to get ignored. Short and sweet please.) Don't give me cultural relativity that is based upon times that aren't relevant at all today. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stating that every other religious or cultural value is either Primitive or childlike is not only absurd, but ethnocentric and offensive to anyone who happens to not be a Western European Christian.</div> </div> </div> </div> What I actually posted. Which was; <i>But I should hope that civilizations and their respective pantheons can do the same. (Of course, that's probably not relevant to the game..*sigh*) Times change...and keeping things as they were thousands of years ago...if not longer, just doesn't make sense to me.</i>...Doesn't look like I used the words &quot;primitive&quot; or &quot;childlike.&quot; (But I have no problem rebutting what you seem to imagine I imply. Although the mods don't like it when I defend myself...<img src=\"http://www.kurts-smilies.de/box.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> So I'll just let it go)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T16:01:33-07:00","id":483981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=483541#post483541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back when civilizations were still in their various beginning stages...yes, I agree.<br /> I look back to when I was a child and see all the mistakes I made. I learned from them and eventually did mature and grow. (and discovered so many new ways to make mistakes..dammit)<br /> But I should hope that civilizations and their respective pantheons can do the same. (Of course, that's probably not relevant to the game..*sigh*) Times change...and keeping things as they were thousands of years ago...if not longer, just doesn't make sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Short &amp; sweet:<br /> <br /> Note, please, &quot;I look back to when I was a child&quot;. Yes, emphatically, you are calling older civilizations childlike. You are implying they, like you, will be better when they &quot;mature and grow&quot;.<br /> <br /> That is a false analogy. Change of cultures over time is not the same as the maturation of a human child. You are mistaking correlation for causation. <br /> <br /> Without bringing in cultural relativity at all, the logical progression of your argument is exactly as Ulf portrays it. <br /> <br /> And, is, in any case, none of this is particularly on point. If I understand the OP correctly, we should be talking about what it really means to be a pantheon. Can a bunch of folks get together eat cheetos, play video games and work with their publicist to make up some fake stories about them call themselves a pantheon? Is their pantheon equivalent to a &quot;stodgy old school&quot; pantheon? Does getting access to a PSP make a difference? Does getting some unused PSP from another pantheon work for or against their argument? <br /> <br /> If not, what DOES it take be a pantheon? Should there be an official-esque definition? Like needed a certain number of Legend 12 gods, a PSP (And how do you come up with one of those? And how do scions buy it? And what happens to any dots in their old PSP?), a set of 4 Virtues (and is it possible for those with different Virtues to join in? If so, how do they go about changing their current Virtues to start matching up with those of the newfangled Pantheon? How many do they have to change?)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T18:27:02-07:00","id":484087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=483981#post483981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Short &amp; sweet:<br /> <br /> Note, please, &quot;I look back to when I was a child&quot;. Yes, emphatically, you are calling older civilizations childlike. You are implying they, like you, will be better when they &quot;mature and grow&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Civilization was in its infancy millennia ago. That seems obvious. Human sacrifices, especially the children...doesn't equate to a mature society as we know it today.<br /> To better illustrate, how does anyone here view &quot;honor killings?&quot; Such a practice was once viewed favorably long ago. Not today. We see it as criminal. And I should think that means we as a society is indeed getting more mature. Better. Women were once chattel/property. Do we think that today? (...some people I suppose..*shrugs*) And another note; slavery...? Really? No. We are better today because we recognize the self-worth of humanity in general.<br /> *shrugs* My opinion won't change yours, no matter how many real-life examples I throw at you. But you aren't able to change my opinion either. Too much history I can point at...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=483981#post483981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, is, in any case, none of this is particularly on point. If I understand the OP correctly, we should be talking about what it really means to be a pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Superheroes-Gods-Comparative-Babylonia-Batman/dp/0786431849\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41K6pz9YBbL.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T18:56:02-07:00","id":484136,"title":"","content":"As ontogeny does not recapitulate phylogeny, neither does maturation model cultural change. That's like thinking evolution has a purpose or a goal instead of simply a direction (which is &quot;forward through time&quot; with nothing about the future being &quot;better&quot; than the past, or even that forward means &quot;more complex&quot;).<br /> <br /> For example: Just look behind the label and you'll see we still have human sacrifice in the variant of modern Western culture we have in America. We call it &quot;capital punishment&quot;. We call it &quot;double blind medical trials&quot;. But there's really no meaningful distinction. All involve the death of a human being against their will to serve a greater good. Except that both of those are perhaps a great deal more cruel than the human sacrifice practiced by most of the ancient cultures typically referenced, as they both involve condemning the sacrifice then postponing the deed, offering false hope, sometimes having the death be exceedingly slow, painful and humiliating, etc. <br /> <br /> You can do the same thing with slavery and women's rights. Some cultures are or were worse at those things than this one. Some are or were much better. If mass enslavement is the alternative to mass genocide, which course is the moral one? Which is the practical one? Which of the two evils is lesser? <br /> <br /> In Scion those answers can be uncomfortably easy. Conviction to the right cause and mass genocide is always preferable to mass enslavement. Or vice versa. With Courage going to war for what we would see as fairly insignificant is de jure. Valor may demand you accept an honorable surrender, but, it may also demand, absent such a surrender, that you kill someone who is effectively defenseless and putting themselves in danger for selfless reasons. (Then your Expression may demand that you laud such a glorious death at your own hands). Etc. Etc. <br /> <br /> What is the point of the book cover? Are you going to precis the book and discuss how it's relevant to the question asked? Are you recommending the book as enlightening on those topics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T17:37:07-08:00","id":1181532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=455062#post455062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Did you just describe Star Wars?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but I admire your snark factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T17:44:27-08:00","id":1181533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=460684#post460684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been told both the Overworld and the Underworld are infinite, so there is plenty of room to carve out new Pantheon territories. Except I've also been told most of the pantheons don't like each other very much, so you'd have that to worry about in addition to the Titans.<br /> <br /> <br /> On another note, I quite like the mental image of a bunch of gods sitting around playing games and eating chips all day while hiring people to write their legends for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh they're fighting the Titans in similar ways to the other pantheons but they use art and media to promote their ideals and valies in the modern world as well. The gods fight the Titans on many levels. Transforming the consciousness and values of the masses to strengthen them against the Titans is simply another ways the Gods guard the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T17:54:59-08:00","id":1181537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/453086-what-if-a-group-of-lesser-immortals-wanted-to-be-a-full-fledged-pantheon?p=478747#post478747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, the Gods can re-write human opinions, easily. An Epic Social here, an Epic Social there, and now hundreds of millions of humans no longer think the Gods are tyrants at all. Scion is not a game where humans matter in the grand scheme of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Epic Socials are best used with subtlety. Forcing humanity to your will is counterproductive. Art and storytelling are potent vectors to work at useing Epic Socials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}